<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis remains firm.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis remains firm.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat remained firm Tuesday as farmer sales stayed slack, dealers in the central U.S. High Plains said.</p>
<p>&quot;Our basis is really firm right now, and I bet it'll go up before it goes down,&quot; an Oklahoma merchandiser said.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, wet fields continued to limit fieldwork in the central Plains.</p>
<p>&quot;Everybody wants to get corn and milo harvested, but they're also wanting to plant,&quot; a Kansas dealer said. &quot;These rains are slowing things down for both harvesting and planting.&quot;  </p>
